# Reverse proxy / TLS termination for Prelude Health.
#
# Not wired to a real host yet -- there is no deployment target as of this
# writing. Replace `:80` below with your actual domain (e.g.
# `prelude-health.example.com`) once one exists; Caddy then issues and
# renews a Let's Encrypt certificate automatically, no manual cert
# lifecycle management required.
#
# `reverse_proxy` handles WebSocket upgrades natively (needed for
# /ws/intake/{session_id}, the live-audio call) -- unlike nginx, no extra
# `Upgrade`/`Connection` header directives are needed here.
#
# For a quick local/LAN test with a self-signed cert instead of a real
# domain, replace the site address with `:443` and add `tls internal`
# inside the block -- note this is NOT production-correct (browsers will
# warn on the self-signed cert), it's only for confirming the proxy wiring
# itself works before a real domain is available.

your-domain.example.com {
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}
